6. Current Viewport Loading / Reconciliation Behavior

loadViewport() in MapComponent:

private loadViewport(): void {
  const bounds = this.map.getBounds();
  this.areaService.getAreas(bounds).subscribe({
    next: (areas) => {
      this.persistedItems.clearLayers();
      areas.forEach((area) => {
        if (area.id === this.editingArea?.id || area.id === this.deletedArea?.id) return;
        this.addPersistedArea(area);
      });
    },
    error: (err) => console.error('Failed to load areas', err),
  });
}

Key properties:
- Uses this.map.getBounds() — reads current viewport at call time, not a cached bbox.
- Calls persistedItems.clearLayers() — full replacement, not a merge. All stale layers are removed before the authoritative response is rendered.
- Skips the area currently in edit (editingArea) and the area showing the delete indicator (deletedArea) to avoid disrupting the in-progress UI state.

This reconciliation correctly handles all missed-event cases (CREATE, UPDATE, DELETE, RESTORE) in one REST call.

