10. Recommended Reconnect Delay / Backoff

Fixed reconnectDelay: 3000 (3 seconds) is sufficient for this assignment. The requirements do not specify SLAs for WebSocket reconnect latency. Three seconds is aggressive enough to reconnect quickly after transient failures and not so aggressive as to create a thundering-herd problem in a single-instance prototype.

Exponential backoff adds code complexity with no clear benefit at this scale. The @stomp/stompjs library does not provide built-in exponential backoff — implementing it manually would require a custom counter and timer. Not warranted.

