No special deduplication is needed. The current implementation creates exactly one subscription per onConnect invocation, and onConnect fires once per successful STOMP session. There is no mechanism that could cause duplicate subscriptions:
- The Client object is replaced only when disconnect() is called followed by a new connect().
- Automatic reconnects reuse the same Client object, and each reconnect fires one onConnect.
- The backend SimpleBroker tracks subscriptions per STOMP session. Each reconnect starts a new session.

