13. Exact Post-Reconnect Reconciliation Flow

1. WebSocket session closes (network loss, timeout, or server restart)
2. @stomp/stompjs schedules reconnect after 3000ms
3. beforeConnect fires:
   a. authService.getToken() → if null: client.deactivate() and return (stop loop)
   b. client.connectHeaders = { Authorization: 'Bearer <current-token>' }
4. @stomp/stompjs opens new WebSocket to ws://localhost:8081/ws
5. @stomp/stompjs sends STOMP CONNECT frame with current token
6. JwtChannelInterceptor validates JWT → success
7. SimpleBroker sends STOMP CONNECTED frame
8. onConnect fires:
   a. client.subscribe('/topic/workspace/{id}', handler) → new subscription created
   b. firstConnect is false → onReconnect() called
   c. loadViewport() called
9. loadViewport():
   a. bounds = map.getBounds() → current viewport at this moment
   b. GET /workspaces/{id}/areas?bbox=<current-bounds> (with current JWT via authInterceptor)
   c. On success:
      - persistedItems.clearLayers()  ← removes stale/deleted areas
      - areas.forEach(area => addPersistedArea(area)) with edit/delete skip guards
   d. On error: console.error (no crash)
10. UI shows authoritative state for current viewport

