16. Unsaved Draw/Edit Interaction

Leaflet layers are separated into four independent FeatureGroups:
- drawnItems — polygon currently being drawn (not yet saved)
- editItems — polygon being edited (not yet saved)
- persistedItems — authoritative saved area layers
- previewItems — history version preview

loadViewport() calls persistedItems.clearLayers() followed by re-population from REST. It does not touch drawnItems, editItems, or previewItems.

An in-progress draw is not affected by reconciliation. drawnItems is untouched.

An in-progress edit is protected in two ways:
1. editItems is not touched.
2. The area being edited (editingArea?.id) is explicitly skipped in the viewport loop: if (area.id === this.editingArea?.id) return;. The editable version in editItems remains visible; the authoritative version from REST is not re-rendered underneath it.

History preview: previewItems is not touched. The preview polygon remains during reconciliation.

No conflict. Reconciliation is safe to call with any of these states active. No change needed here beyond what already exists.

One residual case: the user is editing Area X while disconnected, and another user deletes Area X. After reconnect, loadViewport() returns no Area X (it is deleted). Area X does not appear in persistedItems, but editItems still shows the editable version. When the user tries to save the edit, the backend returns 409 AREA_DELETED. The existing error handler clears the edit and calls loadViewport(). This is the correct behavior and does not require changes.

