17. Reconnect-vs-WebSocket-Event Race Analysis

After reconnect:
1. onConnect fires → subscription created → loadViewport() called (REST GET started)
2. While GET is in flight, another user makes a mutation → STOMP event arrives
3. handleRealtimeEvent calls loadViewport() → second REST GET started
4. Both GETs complete (in any order)

Each loadViewport() call does clearLayers() then full re-population. The last one to complete determines the final display. Both responses are valid authoritative snapshots. No stale data accumulates because full replacement is idempotent at the collection level.

The race is safe. Cosmetically there may be a brief re-render flicker (two clears in quick succession), but no correctness issue. No sequence numbers, no deduplication, no event sourcing needed.

