19. Task 15 Metrics Interaction

Task 15 implemented WebSocketSessionMetrics backed by a ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet(). On SessionConnectedEvent, the session ID is added. On SessionDisconnectEvent, it is removed (idempotent). The gauge never goes negative.

A disconnect/reconnect cycle produces:
- Disconnect: SessionDisconnectEvent → session ID removed → gauge −1
- Reconnect: SessionConnectedEvent → new session ID added → gauge +1

New and old session IDs are different (Spring generates a new one for each WebSocket handshake). No session ID leakage. The gauge is correct across the cycle.

No changes to metrics code for Task 16. The existing WebSocketSessionMetrics handles this correctly by design.

